{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '4172,4197p;5428,5458p;6589,6610p'; nl -ba ../../../poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L6.json | sed -n '11860,11887p'; nl -ba ../../../docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters.json | sed -n '547,571p;720,742p'\"","aggregated_output":"  4172\t## D388 · 2026-11-09 · A material unsigned obligation gets its own signing question beside an open total of its kind\n  4173\t\n  4174\t- Asked: \"一笔重大的、还没签的承诺（比如为 OpenAI 俄亥俄数据中心租约做担保），要不要在已有的'担保总额'问题之外，单独开一个'会不会签'的问题？\"\n  4175\t  Alex chose \"单独开 (Recommended)\".\n  4176\t- **Decided.** A material unsigned obligation that merits a separate investment judgment keeps its own yes/no question on whether\n  4177\t  it is signed by the check date, beside an open question on the total of the same kind. This confirms D248 boundary 1's exception,\n  4178\t  which had not been put to him. A small unsigned obligation, or a deal already signed under a plan tracked by amount, stays evidence\n  4179\t  for the total.\n  4180\t- **Why it matters now.** The c8 dev draws fold the Ohio guarantee into the aggregate in 3 of 3, and q23 of the frozen judgement gold\n  4181\t  asks it. Arm c9 showed that a sentence-level rule flips by send (round log §§48–50).\n  4182\t- **Next.** A structural lever, designed and reviewed by the council before any send. c8 stays in force until a version is shown to\n  4183\t  be better on new, unused articles.\n  4184\t\n  4185\t## D389 · 2026-11-09 · An unsigned obligation is large enough for its own signing question at about 5% of the company's annual profit\n  4186\t\n  4187\t- Asked: \"“多大算大”用什么尺寸？\" The options were 5% of a year's profit (recommended), 1% of annual revenue, or no threshold and stop.\n  4188\t  Alex chose \"一年利润的 5% (Recommended)\", whose stated terms were:\n  4189\t  - \"单笔未签承诺约达到公司一年利润的 5% 才单独开'会不会签'（亏损公司另议）\";\n  4190\t  - \"金额不知道的，比如俄亥俄，仍按文章描述定性判断\";\n  4191\t  - \"公司最近一年利润作为固定资料交给小步骤\".\n  4192\t- **Decided.** Under D388, a single unsigned obligation is large enough for its own signing question when its stated amount is about 5%\n  4193\t  or more of the company's most recent annual profit. An obligation whose amount is not stated is judged qualitatively from what the\n  4194\t  item states. The company's most recent annual profit is supplied to the step as fixed input, with its source. A loss-making company\n  4195\t  is not covered and is decided when one arises.\n  4196\t- **Why.** In the focused D388 call, the same $2bn stake opened in 0 of 3 draws under one wording and 3 of 3 under another, and a\n  4197\t  $2.5–3bn stake opened in 6 of 6, even when compared with stated revenue (round log §§54–55). The standard's \"large enough to change\"\n  5428\t## D480 · 2026-11-13 · Under choice 3, production's opening rule is probed with a price (D191 point 4, D368 item 1) on its stored requests (council consensus under D439)\n  5429\t\n  5430\t- **Loss** (production's largest consistent one): the memory-price question q05, graded, is never opened in 6 of 6 production draws; traced\n  5431\t  at $0 to v74i's \"industry_aggregate: one aggregate quantity for one calendar year …\", which leaves out the price the standard and Alex's\n  5432\t  D191 point 4 include (\"好\"); D368 item 1 (\"这个你记住，我们要做\") ordered it built in the next extraction version, measured against v74i.\n  5433\t- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mu-codex-27.md`): per-attempt settlement; \"candidate kept\", not \"opened\"; any guard\n  5434\t  short of valid sends makes the probe inconclusive; byte and preflight evidence; a blind audit. Each is done\n  5435\t  (`docs/research/2026-11-13-shared-quantity-price/PROBE-DESIGN.md`).\n  5436\t- **Decided:** send the frozen probe: one exact edit of the role (\"one quantity or price outside any one company that several companies move\n  5437\t  on, for one calendar year, such as the combined capital spending of named companies or a raw material's contract price\"), against the stored\n  5438\t  request the same hour, on 30 stored production requests, three sends, about $0.7, a $1.5 ceiling. A pass leads to a council decision on a\n  5439\t  production end-to-end measurement of the new version against v74i; a failure stops this change on this evidence.\n  5440\t\n  5441\t## D481 · 2026-11-13 · The production price change fails and stops; next a $0 census of the opening losses by what the article states (council consensus under D439)\n  5442\t\n  5443\t- **Result** (`docs/research/2026-11-13-shared-quantity-price/RESULT.md`; 180 sends, all valid, $0.25): no memory-price candidate in 45 target\n  5444\t  sends of either arm; the model's account: no defined price measure or calendar year stated in the article; the change cost elsewhere (kept\n  5445\t  candidates 29 → 16; statements dropped with no home 117 → 160).\n  5446\t- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mu-codex-28.md`): \"记录并停止本次失败的措辞修改；开展所提零成本 census，但把'缺少明确指标或期间'作为待核实线索，\n  5447\t  不预先归因于同一次写答案选项，也不预先决定下一结构。\"\n  5448\t- **Decided:** the price edit is not adopted and no second sentence is added on this class now. A $0 census over the graded questions of the\n  5449\t  stored production and clean draws: per question and run, opened or not, in the ruler's shape or not, disputed or not; for each loss, from the\n  5450\t  article and library the model saw, whether it states a relevant number, a defined price series or period, whether it supports a checkable\n  5451\t  question, and any direct evidence of the model's reason; causes may be several or unknown; counted by distinct question and by run.\n  5452\t\n  5453\t## D482 · 2026-11-13 · No further paid test on this ruler today; production stays the default; the measured map goes to Alex (council consensus under D439)\n  5454\t\n  5455\t- **Evidence:** the census of the 36 lost graded question-draws by what the article states\n  5456\t  (`docs/research/2026-11-13-shared-quantity-price/CENSUS-BY-ARTICLE.md`, corrected in rounds 29–30): the \"no defined measure or period\" lead\n  5457\t  fits three (production's q05); the rest are readings under D430 (scoring continues under it), reasonable alternatives, shapes the standard\n  5458\t  does not settle, and one breach (p2's q08 date, whose question is also narrower). The unlinked-fact trace the council proposed was done in\n  6589\t## D543 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the cold reflection on the lean path: D518 stands with its reasons, the choice of system is not made in Alex's place, and no investigation is opened (reflection council consensus)\n  6590\t\n  6591\t- **The council** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-2/`): Claude's own reflection written first\n  6592\t  (`own-reflection.md`); a fresh independent Codex session reading the whole record cold (`handoff-cold.md`, `cold-codex-1.md`);\n  6593\t  one challenge round (`cold-challenge-1.md`, `cold-codex-2.md`). Both readings, made apart, reached the same place.\n  6594\t- **Why the path did not reach its goal (agreed):** the fresh week mixed a difference of product policy with a comparison of\n  6595\t  quality (three of the old system's four covered matters are questions Alex's rule forbids the new system, D505); the evidence\n  6596\t  was too thin to rank answers (one run a system, seven answers against fifteen, readers' bars apart); the work followed each\n  6597\t  newly exposed defect instead of asking whether resolving it would select a system (the dependency stretch is the clearest\n  6598\t  case); and the council often corrected work already framed on a premise that the stored request, an earlier decision or the\n  6599\t  order of events contradicted.\n  6600\t- **Conclusions marked as weaker than they look:** \"no eligible judgement disagrees\" in the July comparison (few were eligible);\n  6601\t  \"36 of 438\" (repeated daily readings on a few question paths, not an error rate); the three unsupported answers with a\n  6602\t  missing stored figure (two matters, cause not shown); the new system's three confirmed missing pairs (a minimum; the one test\n  6603\t  was inconclusive); the dependency connection (a conditional replay; it also removes seven filing links).\n  6604\t- **Decided, citing D439:** D518 stands, restated with its reasons: the old system stays the default and both systems stay,\n  6605\t  for continuity and because the new system's answer-choice step has not passed its tests and it is not integrated with\n  6606\t  production storage. The quality of the two systems' answers is not ranked and **the choice of a foundation is not made in\n  6607\t  Alex's place** (the reviewer withdrew \"carry the old system forward provisionally\" as readable for such a choice). No\n  6608\t  investigation is opened: no bounded test on the record is likely to change the choice at a justified cost, and no narrow\n  6609\t  defect is reopened to postpone it. The two problems that do not depend on the choice stay recorded: related facts reaching\n  6610\t  the question that needs them (no common cause or tested general fix among the known cases), and the judge's amounts with\n 11860\t  \"source_id\": \"v28\"\n 11861\t },\n 11862\t {\n 11863\t  \"question_id\": \"Q29\",\n 11864\t  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA complete final agreements for the announced institutional AI-infrastructure financing platforms by August 15, 2027?\",\n 11865\t  \"due\": \"2027-08-15\",\n 11866\t  \"opened\": \"2026-08-15\",\n 11867\t  \"opened_from\": \"gnews:a66e734cdc6c8f0170fe8471\",\n 11868\t  \"type\": \"yes/no\",\n 11869\t  \"possible_answers\": [\n 11870\t   \"NVIDIA completes final agreements for the platforms by August 15, 2027.\",\n 11871\t   \"NVIDIA has not completed final agreements for the platforms by August 15, 2027.\"\n 11872\t  ],\n 11873\t  \"answer\": \"NVIDIA completes final agreements for the platforms by August 15, 2027.\",\n 11874\t  \"answer_index\": 0,\n 11875\t  \"reasons\": \"The reference is NVIDIA’s announced plan for six financing platforms, conditional on definitive agreements; that intended outcome sits at rung 1, but the announcement is not proof of completion. The evidence still makes completion by August 15, 2027 more likely than non-completion: six firms entered MOUs, NVIDIA said none had refused, SEC guidance may ease a relevant financing constraint, and Broadcom executed a comparable chip-backed financing deal. The counterweight is material: the platforms were still being negotiated and at the MOU stage, with no money raised, and NVIDIA cautioned that preliminary arrangements may not become definitive agreements. Those facts temper confidence but do not move the forecast across the binary boundary; roughly eleven months remain.\",\n 11876\t  \"material\": [\n 11877\t   {\n 11878\t    \"tier\": \"fact\",\n 11879\t    \"speaker\": \"SiliconANGLE / Breaking Analysis\",\n 11880\t    \"original\": \"NVIDIA 2026-08-15\",\n 11881\t    \"input_id\": \"gnews:a66e734cdc6c8f0170fe8471\",\n 11882\t    \"day\": \"2026-08-15\",\n 11883\t    \"summary\": \"NVIDIA signed MOUs with Apollo, BlackRock, Blackstone, Brookfield, Goldman Sachs and KKR to establish financing platforms intended to mobilize more than $500 billion of third-party capital over time.\",\n 11884\t    \"quote\": \"Nvidia signed memorandums of understanding with Apollo, BlackRock, Blackstone, Brookfield, Goldman Sachs and KKR to establish independent financing platforms designed to mobilize more than $500 billion of third-party capital over time.\",\n 11885\t    \"publisher\": \"siliconangle.com\"\n 11886\t   },\n 11887\t   {\n   547\t    \"claude\",\n   548\t    \"codex\"\n   549\t   ],\n   550\t   \"articles\": [\n   551\t    3,\n   552\t    9,\n   553\t    20,\n   554\t    48,\n   555\t    56,\n   556\t    60,\n   557\t    95,\n   558\t    105,\n   559\t    146,\n   560\t    149,\n   561\t    187,\n   562\t    189,\n   563\t    214,\n   564\t    215,\n   565\t    224,\n   566\t    277,\n   567\t    398\n   568\t   ],\n   569\t   \"first_day\": \"2026-09-07\",\n   570\t   \"company_figure\": false,\n   571\t   \"company_figure_mixed\": false\n   720\t  },\n   721\t  {\n   722\t   \"matter\": \"M27\",\n   723\t   \"question\": \"How much of NVIDIA's agreed Hugging Face acquisition obligation remains outstanding at FY2027 year-end?\",\n   724\t   \"name\": \"NVIDIA Hugging Face acquisition obligation at FY2027 year-end\",\n   725\t   \"entries\": [\n   726\t    30\n   727\t   ],\n   728\t   \"entry_names\": [\n   729\t    \"NVIDIA Hugging Face acquisition obligation at FY2027 year-end\"\n   730\t   ],\n   731\t   \"listed_by\": [\n   732\t    \"codex\"\n   733\t   ],\n   734\t   \"articles\": [\n   735\t    3,\n   736\t    9,\n   737\t    20,\n   738\t    277,\n   739\t    398\n   740\t   ],\n   741\t   \"first_day\": null,\n   742\t   \"company_figure\": false,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,re,sys; sys.path.insert(0,\\\".\\\"); import judge_probe as p; f=p.ROOT/\\\"docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/numbering.json\\\"; ids=json.loads(f.read_text()); db=p.readonly(p.DIAG.parent/\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\");\nfor k in (\\\"259\\\",\\\"322\\\",\\\"398\\\"):\n row=db.execute(\\\"select title,text from items where input_id=?\\\",(ids[k],)).fetchone(); print(k,ids[k],row[\\\"title\\\"]);\n for a in re.split(r\\\"(?<=[.\"'!?])'\"\\\\s+\\\", \\\" \\\".join((row[\\\"text\\\"] or \\\"\\\").split())):\n  if re.search(r\\\"pick up more strongly|major contributor|residual-value support|agreed last month|definitive agreement|first half of 2027|approval\\\",a,re.I): print(a[:460]);\n if k==\\\"322\\\":\n  v=p.readonly(p.store_paths(\\\"old-1\\\")[0]); h=json.loads(v.execute(\\\"select handover_json from handovers where input_id=?\\\",(ids[k],)).fetchone()[0]); print([(x[\\\"one_line\\\"],x[\\\"links\\\"]) for x in h[\\\"evidence\\\"] if \\\"residual-value support\\\" in x[\\\"one_line\\\"]]);\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,re,sys; sys.path.insert(0,\\\".\\\"); import judge_probe as p; f=p.ROOT/\\\"docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/numbering.json\\\"; ids=json.loads(f.read_text()); db=p.readonly(p.DIAG.parent/\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\");\nfor k in (\\\"259\\\",\\\"322\\\",\\\"398\\\"):\n row=db.execute(\\\"select title,text from items where input_id=?\\\",(ids[k],)).fetchone(); print(k,ids[k],row[\\\"title\\\"]);\n for a in re.split(r\\\"(?<=[.\"'!?])'\"\\\\s+\\\", \\\" \\\".join((row[\\\"text\\\"] or \\\"\\\").split())):\n  if re.search(r\\\"pick up more strongly|major contributor|residual-value support|agreed last month|definitive agreement|first half of 2027|approval\\\",a,re.I): print(a[:460]);\n if k==\\\"322\\\":\n  v=p.readonly(p.store_paths(\\\"old-1\\\")[0]); h=json.loads(v.execute(\\\"select handover_json from handovers where input_id=?\\\",(ids[k],)).fetchone()[0]); print([(x[\\\"one_line\\\"],x[\\\"links\\\"]) for x in h[\\\"evidence\\\"] if \\\"residual-value support\\\" in x[\\\"one_line\\\"]]);\n'\"","aggregated_output":"259 gnews:5c5a96c670714dee86769d87 Why It’s Time to Load Up on Nvidia Stock\nNvidia's data center operations are positioned to remain a major contributor, particularly as customers continue adopting the Blackwell architecture.\n322 gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 Analysis: What Nvidia’s Massive Supply-Demand Gap Says About AI Mania\nFor instance, the company agreed last month to provide a guarantee of up to $105 billion for a massive data center in Ohio that will be leased to OpenAI, with payments by Nvidia set to trigger in case the frontier AI lab defaulted on the lease or failed to make lease payments, according to a filing with the U.S.\nThe AI infrastructure giant may also put up as much as $125 billion in “residual-value support” for partnerships with several Wall Street heavyweights, including Goldman Sachs and Blackstone, which plan to pool $500 billion in capital for AI infrastructure buying.\n[('CRN reported that NVIDIA may provide up to $125 billion of residual-value support for partnerships with Goldman Sachs, Blackstone, and other financial firms planning to pool $500 billion for AI-infrastructure purchases.', ['v2', 'v29'])]\n398 gnews:7a5002df93385ecef12a2cd8 NVIDIA to Acquire Hugging Face for Approximately $12.7 Billion in Strategic Pivot After Earlier Investment Rejection\nThe deal requires regulatory approval from U.S.\nA definitive agreement was signed on September 2, 2026, and CEO Jensen Huang disclosed the deal in an official blog post on September 3.\nDeal completion is targeted for the first half of 2027, but approvals from regulators in multiple jurisdictions, including the EU, are also required.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"**Keep old in production and pause the hybrid release line.** No opening send currently earns its cost. I agree with that exit, with two corrections to the census.\n\n- **M12.** The signed Ohio guarantee belongs under the tracked AI-cloud total unless the annual filing gives analysts a separately meaningful Ohio balance. D210 specifies how to ask about an obligation’s amount. D248 and D388 determine whether it gets a separate question. The trace establishes no need for one here. [D248](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2959) · [D388](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4176)\n- **M27.** A deal that closes in May 2027 can satisfy M19 and still have an outstanding obligation at January year-end. A delay or termination also does not establish that $12.9B remains payable. Classify M27 as **separately answerable in principle, with the public settlement source unproven**. Leave it out of the attainable gains for now. [Frozen matters](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters.json:722)\n- **M07 and M16.** M07’s segment forecast is distinct from total revenue. The lack of a stated figure does not bar it, but the qualitative demand evidence does not establish a missed opening. M16 remains allowed. Exclude the failed wording change from the ceiling until a different mechanism has evidence behind it. [Frozen prompt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt:13) · [D481](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:5441)\n- **M20.** I meant old-1 **Q29 (`v29`)**. The stored $125B statement links directly to it. Q29 asks about platform agreements by August 15. Those agreements could be signed without the specific residual-value support M20 asks about by March 31. The broader question does not settle it. [Old-1 Q29](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L6.json:11863)\n\n**Recommend option 2 to Alex.** Five speculative gains with zero losses can pass mathematically. The two concrete opportunities cannot carry that result. Drop the M20 account probe for release purposes. Widen company coverage only if Alex wants those forecasts for their own value. D543 supports closing the release investigation when another test would leave the decision unchanged. [D543](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:6604)\n\nDISAGREE"}}
